  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">P.O.W.E.R People and Organisations Working for Equality and Rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program P.O.W.E.R. &#x2013; People and Organizations Working for Equality and Rights has been developed by feminists in Lebanon, Human Rights Defenders (HRDs) in Peru, youth mobilisers in Burkina Faso, democracy activists in Sri Lanka, students in Zimbabwe, climate and environmental advocates in Bangladesh, and many more civil society actors across the world. A total of 88 formal and non-formal civil society actors from 19 countries have joined local and global Diakonia staff in co-creation workshops to reflect, analyze and strategize to create the proposed program.</narrative>
  </description>
